70. ŋuruš-ra e₂ nu-nam-ma {urud}ha-zi-in šu ŋal₂ ba-ši-in-ti
#lem: ŋuruš[young adult male]; e[house]; me[be]; hazin[ax]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: They sharpened their daggers, they smashed his hut. 
#etcsl: line-id=70

71. ŋiri₂-ur₃-ra mu-ni-in-sar-sar-re-eš ki-sig₉-ga mu-ni-in-dub₂-eš
#lem: ŋiriʾurak[knife]; sar[sharpen]; kisiga[fence]; dub[tremble]
#tr.en: His sister wandered about the city like a bird because of her brother: 
#etcsl: line-id=71

72. nin₉-e %e na-aŋ₂ %s šeš-na-še₃ iri-a mušen-gin₇ im-ma-an-niŋin₂-niŋin₂
#lem: nin[sister]; naŋ[fate]N; šeš[brother]; iri[city]; mušen[bird]; niŋin[encircle]
#tr.en: @q[Jectin-ana,Dumuzid]{“My brother, let me take the great misfortune, come, 
